+## Subtopics
+
+### Sensitivity-Aware Vector Clustering
+Groups Gaussians based on rendering sensitivity to reduce redundancy. Choose when geometric simplification is preferred over transmission optimization. [Link](12167-sensitivity-aware-vector-clustering.md)
+
+### Compact 3D Gaussian Representation (C3DGS)
+Reduces storage by optimizing the Gaussian representation itself (e.g., shared codebooks). Choose when memory footprint is the primary constraint. [Link](12927-compact-3d-gaussian-representation-c3dgs.md)
+
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Encoding/Decoding is $O(1)$ per number, but matrix traversal for color compression is $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of elements, and is identified as a bottleneck [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Reduces storage size by replacing multi-byte floats/ints with single ASCII characters (1 byte) where applicable [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Performance:** Gains approximately 6% or less in training speed [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Simple implementation; reduces data transmission size.
-*   **Limitations:** Limited range for integer/floating-point components (0-95); color matrix compression is slow due to traversal overhead; limited overall speedup [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** The compression/decompression is $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of parameters. However, matrix traversal for color compression is a bottleneck. Using `torch.where` and `torch.index_select` mitigates this but remains slower than native binary operations [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Reduces storage size by encoding multiple values into single ASCII characters. The color matrix reduction is significant due to quantization [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Performance:** Gains approximately 6% or less improvement in training speed [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Strengths:** Improves data transmission speed; simple implementation using standard ASCII libraries.
+*   **Limitations:** Not fast enough for full replacement of matrix operations; precision loss in color quantization; delimiter handling adds overhead [S1, unofficial].
+*   **When to use:** When data transmission is the bottleneck in training and minor precision loss is acceptable.
+*   **When not to use:** When maximum rendering fidelity is required or when matrix traversal speed is critical.
 
 ## Background
-This method was proposed in the context of improving 3D Gaussian Splatting training speed by optimizing data transmission [S1, unofficial]. It is part of the "Anywhere" compression approach described in the I3DGS paper [S1, unofficial].
+This method was introduced in the paper "I3DGS: Improve 3D Gaussian Splatting from Multiple Dimensions" [S1, unofficial]. It is part of a broader effort to optimize 3D Gaussian Splatting training speed through various dimensions including color, learning, structure design, and compression [S1, unofficial].
 
